  "stood_definition": "STOOD iff (1) last 3.0 s (150 control steps): on EVERY step the chassis box's lowest point >= 0.10 m above the table-top plane (z >= 0.735 m), AND on >= 95 % of the steps (>= 143 of 150) >= 5 of 6 footpads loaded on the floor (net contact >= 20 N, footpad centre z <= 0.15 m; the tolerance absorbs post-settle load flickers); (2) whole episode: body tilt (body z vs world z) <= 0.5 rad (else FALL); (3) whole episode: the chassis' lowest point never below the table-top plane by more than 0.05 m (else FELL OFF THE TABLE); (4) no termination (only a time-out 2 s past the episode remains). Reported, not gated: stood_strict (>= 5 feet on EVERY window step), the window share of steps with >= 5 feet and the window's min feet, lift-off (belly gap > 0.02 m held 0.5 s), final root z / gap / feet, max tilt, cams homed at the end (worst |cam| <= 0.10 rad).",
